<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Bundu</h1><p class="st-meta">1690 CE – 1905 CE (approx.) · capital Boulebane</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Muslim clerical state between the Senegal and Faleme rivers, among the earliest of its kind in West Africa and a forerunner of the later Fulbe imamates.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Bundu was founded around 1690 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-sy">Malik Sy</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toroodbe">Torodbe</a> cleric from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imamate-of-futa-toro">Futa Toro</a>, who obtained land from the ruler of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gajaaga">Kingdom of Gajaaga</a> and drew settlers to his community. He is remembered by the clerical title eliman; his descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisibe">Sisibe</a>, ruled after him and later took the title almamy. Its creation came a generation before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihads</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imamate-of-futa-jallon">Futa Jallon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/futa-toro">Futa Toro</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Bundu was governed by almamys of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisibe">Sisibe</a> lineage, whose succession was often contested between rival branches. Its towns, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulebane">Boulebane</a> and Koussan among them, were centres of Islamic learning. Lying near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bambuk">Bambuk</a> goldfields and on the routes from the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-gambia">Gambia</a>, it profited from caravans of gold, slaves, cloth and salt, and it warred repeatedly with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaarta">Kaarta</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-khasso">Khasso</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gajaaga">Gajaaga</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 1850s Bundu was caught between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-hadj-umar-tall">Umar Tall</a> and the French. Almamy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bokar-saada">Bokar Saada</a> sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and Bundu became a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in the 1880s before being absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-senegal">French Senegal</a>, its almamys reduced to local chiefs by about 1905.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="theocracy, 1690 CE – 1905 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 82 V46 Q50 12 70 46 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 30 V82 M40 58 H60"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">theocracy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.33%;width:4.28%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1690 CE – 1905 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Boulebane</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Malik Sy, Bokar Saada</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pulaar, Soninke</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/senegal">Senegal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bundu, Bondu, Boundou</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bundu" aria-label="Kingdom of Bundu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4272 1618 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Bundu lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M4830 1933h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4592 1874h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4592 1874h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Senegal. <a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bundu">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

